I built the sprint board in React 19 and TypeScript. `./check` is clean and all 26 visible tests pass in `./test` (2 of the 15 runs used). There is one console error, a 404 for some resource, which I didn't look into; it is probably the missing favicon.

**How it works:** each page keeps its own small store, which is created again whenever the page opens. Every change (move, add, rename, archive, toggle, add item, restore) is shown at once as a pending change on top of what the server has confirmed. When the server answers, an accepted change becomes part of the confirmed data and a declined one is simply dropped. So when several requests are in flight and one fails, only that one is undone. Late answers for a column or checklist load that has been replaced are ignored. Loads are never sent twice, even under `StrictMode`.

**Choices the brief left open:**
- Move buttons are disabled while the destination column is loading or has failed.
- Pending "(adding…)" cards count as positions for `up`/`down` and in the bottom index sent to the server.
- Titles and item text are trimmed before sending.
- `title-input` keeps its text after a rename; only the add inputs are emptied.
- Clicking the card that is already selected does nothing. Selecting any other card always loads its checklist again.

The code is in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-react-opus-4/src/`: `App.tsx`, `Board.tsx`, `Archive.tsx`, `boardStore.ts`, `archiveStore.ts` and `styles.ts`.